# Sit down, lie down in Russian: сесть, лечь, встать
subtitle: "Сидеть or сесть, лежать or лечь: the Russian verbs for being in a position and for moving into it, with где and куда."
tags: ["russian","сесть лечь встать","verbs of position","russian verbs","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/verbs-of-position","vocabulary/body"]
thumb: "band \"Lie down, in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"The city where I was born in Russian: город, где…","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/162-russian-where-i-was-born.cast"}

## Sit down, lie down in Russian: сесть, лечь, встать
stress: new
